Step 1: Add Devices

Open Cisco Packet Tracer.

Go to Network Devices → Wireless Devices.

Select WRT300N (Wireless Router) and drag it into the workspace.

Go to End Devices.

Add three laptops to the workspace.

Step 2: Configure Wireless Router

Click WRT300N Wireless Router.

Open the GUI tab.

Select Wireless → Basic Wireless Settings.

Configure the following:

Network Mode: Mixed

Network Name (SSID): College_wifi

Standard Channel: 6

SSID Broadcast: Enabled

Click Save Settings.

Step 3: Configure WPA2-PSK Security

Go to Wireless → Wireless Security.

Select Security Mode: WPA2 Personal.

Select Encryption: AES.

Enter Passphrase: college12345.

Click Save Settings.

Step 4: Install Wireless Adapter in Laptop 1

Click Laptop 1.

Open the Physical tab.

Switch OFF the laptop using its power button.

Select WPC300N from the module list.

Drag and drop WPC300N into the empty module slot.

Switch ON the laptop.

Step 5: Configure Other Laptops
Repeat Step 4 for Laptop 2 and Laptop 3 to install the WPC300N wireless adapter.

Step 6: Connect Laptop 1 to Wireless Router

Click Laptop 1.

Open Desktop → PC Wireless.

Select the Connect tab.

Select College_wifi from the available wireless networks.

Click Connect.

Select WPA2-Personal if prompted.

Enter the password college12345.

Click Connect.

Step 7: Connect Laptop 2 and Laptop 3
Repeat Step 6 for Laptop 2 and Laptop 3 using the same SSID and password.

Step 8: Assign IP Addresses

Click Laptop 1.

Open Desktop → IP Configuration.

Select DHCP.

Check the automatically assigned IP address.

Repeat for Laptop 2 and Laptop 3.

Step 9: Test Connectivity Using Ping

Open Laptop 1 → Desktop → Command Prompt.

Enter ping 192.168.0.1 to test connectivity with the wireless router.

Ping the IP addresses of Laptop 2 and Laptop 3.

Check whether successful replies are received.

Step 10: Test Unauthorized Access

Open PC Wireless → Connect on a laptop.

Select College_wifi.

Enter an incorrect password, such as wrong12345.

Click Connect.

Verify that the laptop cannot connect using the incorrect password.

